            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 1)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "5627dc6e-c943-439e-ab4a-4531b7f24264"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Establishment of the PLO</strong><br>\nThe Palestine Liberation Organization, or PLO for short, was founded in 1964. Its aim was to create a national representation for the Palestinian people and to fight for their rights and independence. The PLO demanded the right to self-determination and the establishment of an independent state of Palestine.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Structure</strong><br>\nThe PLO has a complex political structure with various factions and groups. The Palestinian National Council is the PLO's highest decision-making body and consists of representatives from various Palestinian organizations. The PLO's executive is led by the Executive Committee, which makes political decisions and coordinates the organization's activities.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Military Actions</strong><br>\nIn the 1970s and 1980s, the PLO, often through its military wings such as Fatah, targeted military and civilian objectives in Israel and other countries. These attacks led to international condemnation and an ongoing conflict with Israel. The PLO stated that these actions were necessary to draw attention to the oppression of the Palestinian people.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Oslo Accords</strong><br>\nThe PLO was a central figure in the Oslo Accords of 1993 and 1995, which established a framework for future relations between Palestinians and Israelis. The accords led to Israel's recognition of the PLO and the establishment of the Palestinian Authority, which received certain self-governing powers.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Second Intifada</strong><br>\nThe Second Intifada, which began in 2000, was a period of increased violence between Israelis and Palestinians. The PLO and its factions were involved in many of the conflicts and attacks. This led to a deterioration in relations between the two parties and a significant worsening of the situation in the region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Recognition on the International Stage</strong><br>\nOver the years, the PLO has gained some recognition on the international stage. Many countries and international organizations have recognized the PLO as the legitimate representation of the Palestinian people. This has enabled the PLO to advocate for Palestinian rights internationally and gather support.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
